Apple today released visionOS 27.2, the first big update for the visionOS 27 operating system that runs on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-vision-pro/">Apple Vision Pro</a>. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2024/03/apple-vision-pro-orange.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-944159" /><br/>
visionOS 27.2 can be downloaded by opening the Settings app, selecting the General section, and choosing Software Update. Installing the update requires the headset to be removed, and a progress bar appears on the EyeSight display.<br/>
<br/>
The visionOS 27.2 update provides bug fixes and security updates, per Apple's release notes. <br/>
